#+TITLE: CAD vendor-probe campaign (drive the real-CAD-gated CAD-runtime issues)
#+STATUS: WIP
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: ci-campaign
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: cad-vendor-probe-campaign

* Why

The macOS (BricsCAD) and Windows (AutoCAD + BricsCAD) runners are available
again (pjb, 2026-09-26), so the CAD-hardware-gated CAD-runtime issues can be
driven to closure through the native child pipeline (.gitlab/native.yml). This
issue tracks that campaign; each target issue is closed on its own evidence.

* Targets and the job that informs each

- autocad-runtime-vlax-sleep-and-rest — code complete (1.6.4/1.6.6), open only
  pending a confirming run. Job: =vendor:probes:autocad= (protocol loop holds
  at READY, real verdicts, no unbound-vlax-sleep crash). Close if green.

- autocad-no-rest-output-capture — the -x / native-load eval-request path loses
  CAD output. First PROBE whether accoreconsole honours LOGFILEMODE /
  LOGFILEPATH under /isolate (a small probe form via
  =probe:suite:autocad:windows= or a dedicated run), then implement the capture
  (route -x through source-load, or tee the command-line log), then re-verify.

- accoreconsole-deported-load-highbyte — a source file with a high byte (é=0xE9)
  fails LOAD under accoreconsole (LISPSYS 0, ANSI_1252). Job:
  =encoding:experiment:autocad:windows= (scripts/run-encoding-experiment.ps1
  -Backend autocad) to reproduce; then bring autolisp-source-load to the
  encoding-honouring reference loader and re-run (LISPSYS 0 vs 1/2, no /isolate).

* Also validates (residual of the now-closed vla-* issues)

- =probe:suite:autocad:windows= / =vendor:probes:bricscad:macos= exercise the
  SPEC-UNCERTAIN vendor behaviours the two closed vla-* issues left to confirm
  (EffectiveName on dynamic blocks, entmakex-on-BLOCK, ENDBLK-terminated entnext
  walk, glyph-metric bounding boxes). Findings feed deferred-spec-research.issue
  and the autolisp-spec divergence notes; no code is blocked on them.

* Log

- 2026-09-26: campaign opened; MR spawns the native child; playing the AutoCAD
  and BricsCAD probe jobs. (Results appended as they return.)

** 2026-09-26 — first probe round + bridge fix

detect:runners: MACOS_RUNNER=online, WINDOWS_RUNNER=online. Native child
2885655529 ran the AutoCAD/BricsCAD probes. Findings:

- BLOCKER FOUND (alfe 2.2.107): vendor:probes:autocad failed before READY with
  bridge-autocad.vbs(138,1) "Variable non definie: 'lastTouchError'" — every
  AutoCAD probe then reported "backend unreachable" (3 probes failed). The
  bridge's Option Explicit script assigns lastTouchError (the hung-instance
  retry, alfe-autocad-hung-instance-blocks-com-bootstrap) but never Dim'd it.
  FIX: added lastTouchError to the Dim in backend-autocad.lisp; added a headless
  regression test (autocad-bridge-template-declares-every-global-under-option-
  explicit) that lints the emitted template for any Option-Explicit global
  assigned-but-not-Dim'd. alfe suite 1202/1202. Relates to
  alfe-autocad-vbscript-comments. This unblocks #4 verification and the AutoCAD
  vla SPEC-UNCERTAIN probes on the next run.

- #5 accoreconsole-deported-load-highbyte REPRODUCED: encoding:experiment:
  autocad:windows shows source.{default,utf8,utf16le}.load = LOAD-ERR for a file
  containing (setq ENCSRC "A<e9>Z") across chcp 1252/437, UTF-8, C — while plain
  open+read-char reads the bytes fine (file.default.hex = 41 e9 ac 42). So the
  deported source-load chokes on the high byte specifically; the probe masks the
  real error as LOAD-ERR. NEXT: surface the actual error message, then bring
  autolisp-source-load to the encoding-honouring reference loader.
